  c-api-growth: DECIDED (VD, 2026-07-10), window: pre-release -
    both frozen-surface extensibility jobs as one item. (1) Output
    channels: a new-named dbarts_sampler_run2 taking an extended
    results struct whose FIRST member is a caller-set size/version;
    the library never writes past the declared size; fields append
    monotonically (version = layout revision, NOT model type);
    per-model variability stays on the existing null-pointer
    opt-in convention (irrelevant channels simply never fill).
    (2) State format: additive by-name blocks - the state is
    already marshaled as named R objects, so the reader looks up
    blocks by name, defaults absent OPTIONAL blocks, and refuses
    (naming the block) only when a REQUIRED one is missing; the
    version stamp stays for provenance, not gatekeeping. Preserves
    the never-silently-misinterpret safety while ending the
    every-change-orphans-all-states behavior. Absorbs
    flat-format-v2. Medium; land before 1.0-0 submission.
